# Committed configs are hashed byte-for-byte into every result's provenance
# (temper/eval/provenance.py: config_digest). Line endings are bytes. The M2
# results were stamped from a Windows checkout, where core.autocrlf gave the
# configs CRLF endings, so CRLF is pinned here for every platform: a Linux clone
# now reproduces the committed digests instead of failing the invariant-1 checks
# on an invisible byte. Everything else follows the platform default.
configs/*.yaml text eol=crlf
